## @SunStarSys/orion

- NKOTB

## @GoHugoIo/hugo

- Popular
- Robust Third-Party Themes and Extensions
- Opinionated w/ Steep Learning Curve

## Common Feature Sets

- Apache Licensed
- High Performance (max document processing speed at ~1K documents per second)
- Cached Dependency Management
- Sophisticated Security Model

## Orion Advantages

1. {# lede #}(Configurable) Full power of Django Templates within Markdown sources{# lede #}
2. Robust Control Flow, For-Loop Constructs, and Django Filters
3. Full Access To YAML/CSV attached documents as data structures
4. Vector Graphics
5. Vector Operations on CSV Table Data via `PDL`
6. `ssi` skips file headers
7. MultiViews
8. Easy to Use
9. Flexible, True Incremental Builds
10. Per-file/directory (aka fine-grained) ACL, including controls on the build's software stack and configuration itself

### CMS Editor

<center>

![Editor X](ssg.page/screenshot)

</center>

1. Document Upload Linting based on MIME-type (Markdown, Perl, YAML, CSV, $$\LaTeX$$)
2. Automatic Link Validation / Titleization
3. Real Time Preview Rendering for `@`-shortlinks (eg :fa-x-twitter: tweets)
4. Electric HTML/Tab Completion
5. Multilingual w/ AI translation capabilities &mdash; including Chinese, Hebrew and Arabic

### Incremental Builds

#### O(N) vs. O(1)

#### Hugo's Primitive Dependency Cache (aka Gilding the Lilly)

https://deepwiki.com/gohugoio/hugo/3.6-dependency-tracking-and-caching

- inflexible, internally generated [**DAG**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Directed_acyclic_graph) based on node/leaf/bundle tree layouts
- never written to disk

##### Hugo's untracked `readFile` calls break incremental build support

https://mbuege.com/2025/09/04/hugo-include-shortcode/

```mermaid
treeView-beta
    archetypes/
    assets/
    content/
      includes/
        dummy.md :::highlight ## untracked dependency in Hugo
      posts/
        2025-01-01-post1.md  ## may use "include" shortcodes
        2025-01-02-post2.md  ## ...
    data/
    i18n/
    layouts/
      shortcodes/
        include.html  ## uses readFile() on a passed argument
    static/
    themes/
```

*Hugo does not track content dependencies that arise from shortcodes, and makes rigid DAG assumptions about the content dependencies it does track.*

##### Orion's fully tracked `ssi` calls

```mermaid
treeView-beta
trunk/
   content/
     foo/
	   fileA.md.en :::highlight ## target include file
	 bar/
	   fileB.md.en ## `ssi` includes select portions of fileA.md.en
   cgi-bin/
   lib/
   templates/
```

*Orion natively tracks `fileB.md.en`'s dependency on `fileA.md.en` and will rebuild it whenever `fileA.md.en` is altered; and dependencies are configurable per document, not assumed by heirarchical structure.*

Orion's Dependency graph is **almost never a DAG**:

[![not a DAG](../images/deps.svg{{lang}})](dependencies)

