### Version Control

#### Git and Fine-Grained ACLs

Impossible in any DVCS &mdash; read access to the repository implies access to its entirety, including history.  Ditto for push access: it is all-or-nothing, which is a deal-breaker in a wiki context where different repository users require granular file/directory write authorization/access controls.

#### Subversion

Trivial **per-user integration** with git/GitHub via `git-svn` bridge.

